{
  "0": "Feature construction: scale each input item embedding by clip((median_train_count/max(train_count[item],1))^0.1,0.8,1.2), using category-specific counts from training interactions only. Mild frequency normalization may expose informative niche purchases, particularly in Electronics, without overwhelming common-item signals. Preserve embedding parameters, GRU, readout, scoring, loss and optimizer; save these fixed feature scales and apply them identically in the predictor.",
  "1": "Training strategy: change only the learning-rate schedule to a two-epoch linear warmup from 0.1 times the existing learning rate, followed by cosine decay to 0.1 times that rate at epoch 200. Smoother initial updates and gradual decay may reduce the observed validation oscillation while retaining later learning in CDs_and_Vinyl. Preserve optimizer type, batch size, early stopping, dropout, weight decay, model, loss, sampling and seeds; use no additional training runs.",
  "2": "Learning objective: replace the current prediction loss with mean softplus(s_negative - s_positive), using exactly the existing positive examples and sampled negatives, averaging over negatives before examples. Directly optimizing positive-negative score margins may improve HR@10, especially in Electronics. Preserve features, embeddings, GRU, readout, scoring, optimizer, sampling and training settings; train one model per category.",
  "3": "Interest aggregation: replace the current recurrent-state readout with 0.8*h_last + 0.2*sum(w_t*h_t), where normalized weights over valid states are proportional to 2^(-(last-t)/5). This fixed, inexpensive pooling may stabilize the latest interest with recent context while limiting stale-history influence. Preserve history selection, embeddings, GRU topology, candidate scoring, loss and optimizer; implement identical pooling in the predictor, loading one checkpoint per category."
}
